<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oswald of Northumbria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 604–<a href="/years/642">642</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saint Oswald</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oswald was king of Northumbria from 634 to 642. A son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelfrith-of-northumbria">Æthelfrith of Bernicia</a>, he spent his youth in exile among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaels">Gaels</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a> and became a Christian on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iona">Iona</a>. He won the throne by defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cadwallon-ap-cadfan">Cadwallon of Gwynedd</a> at Heavenfield, brought the monk Aidan from Iona to found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lindisfarne">Lindisfarne</a>, and was killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a> at Maserfield in 642. He was venerated as a saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oswald-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="Oswald of Northumbria" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Robin Widdison at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saint_Oswald_Durham_Cathedral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
